# FCC: OpenRouter Gateway

**FCC: OpenRouter Gateway** is a standalone proxy and management product that seamlessly bridges the official [Claude Code CLI](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/agents-and-tools/claude-code/overview) with OpenRouter. 

It provides an out-of-the-box, user-friendly experience with automatic API key rotation, a modern web dashboard, and simple one-command installation. Say goodbye to manual `.env` file editing and complex setup procedures!

*Note: This project originated from [Alishahryar1/free-claude-code](https://github.com/Alishahryar1/free-claude-code) and has been transformed into a fully managed, easy-to-install product.*

## 🚀 Features

- **One Command Install**: Installs all required tools and dependencies automatically.
- **One Command Start**: `fcc-start` handles launching the server, opening the dashboard, and starting Claude Code.
- **OpenRouter Multi-Key Rotation**: Built-in support for rotating multiple OpenRouter API keys to handle rate limits and exhausted balances automatically.
- **Modern Web Dashboard**: A beginner-friendly, clean UI to manage keys, monitor server health, and check provider status.
- **Web-Based Setup**: No more editing `.env` files manually. Just paste your keys in the onboarding screen!
- **Built-in Diagnostics**: Run `fcc-doctor` to instantly find and fix configuration issues.
- **OpenRouter Manager**: Track how many keys are healthy, exhausted, or active in real-time.

## 📦 Installation

To get started, you just need Python installed. Then run our universal installation command:

```bash
uv tool install git+https://github.com/Alishahryar1/free-claude-code.git
```
*(If you don't use `uv`, you can install via pip: `pip install git+https://github.com/Alishahryar1/free-claude-code.git`)*

Once installed, verify the installation by running:
```bash
fcc-install
```

## 🏁 First Run & Setup

Starting the gateway is as simple as:

```bash
fcc-start
```

**What happens?**
1. If you haven't configured OpenRouter keys yet, the server will start and automatically open the **Onboarding Dashboard** in your browser.
2. Paste your OpenRouter API keys (one per line) and click **Apply Configuration**.
3. Click **Start Claude Code**. FCC will spawn a new terminal for the server and launch Claude Code seamlessly!

## 🔧 Configure OpenRouter

1. Run `fcc-start`.
2. Navigate to the **OpenRouter Manager** in the Dashboard (http://localhost:8082/admin).
3. Paste your keys in the Manage Keys text area.
4. Click **Save Keys**. The system will validate and deduplicate your keys. Your changes apply immediately with zero downtime.

## 📊 Dashboard

The FCC Dashboard is your control center.
- **Dashboard**: High-level view of Server Status, loaded OpenRouter keys, and your active provider.
- **OpenRouter Manager**: Monitor key rotation metrics (Total, Healthy, Exhausted, Active Index) and manage your API keys.
- **Provider Status**: Check connectivity to local or remote AI providers.
- **System Status**: View host, port, and system-level diagnostics.

## 🔄 OpenRouter Rotation

Our intelligent rotation system ensures your workflows are never interrupted:
- **Healthy Keys**: Keys that are actively being used and returning successful responses.
- **Exhausted Keys**: Keys that have run out of credits (HTTP 402). They are marked exhausted and skipped.
- **Rotation Logic**: If a key hits a rate limit (HTTP 429), the system automatically rotates to the next healthy key and retries your prompt invisibly.

## 💻 CLI Commands

The gateway provides five core commands for complete control:

- `fcc-install`: Verifies your environment (Python, uv, Git, Claude Code) and sets up required directories.
- `fcc-start`: The main entry point. Checks configuration, starts the proxy server, and launches Claude Code.
- `fcc-status`: Displays the current version, server status, and real-time OpenRouter rotation metrics.
- `fcc-doctor`: Runs a full diagnostic check on your environment to find missing dependencies or broken configurations.
- `fcc-update`: Pulls the latest version from the repository and safely reinstalls while preserving your configuration.

## 🔄 Updating

Updating is safe and preserves your keys and configuration:

```bash
fcc-update
```

## 🛠️ Troubleshooting

- **Missing Claude Code**: If `fcc-doctor` reports Claude Code is missing, install it via `npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code`.
- **Port Conflicts**: Ensure port 8082 is free. If the server fails to start, check the logs or try restarting your terminal.
- **Invalid Keys**: If Claude Code returns an authentication error, verify your keys in the OpenRouter Manager. Exhausted keys will be automatically skipped.
- **Server Errors**: Run `fcc-status` to see if the server is healthy. If stopped, run `fcc-start` again.

## 🏗️ Architecture

```text
User
 ↓ (runs fcc-start)
CLI
 ↓ (checks keys, spawns server)
FCC Server
 ↓ (intercepts API requests)
OpenRouter Manager
 ↓ (rotates keys on 402/429)
OpenRouter
 ↓ (processes request)
Claude Code (in current terminal)
```

## 📚 Migration Guide

If you used older versions of `free-claude-code`, simply install this update. Your `.env` files will be preserved. However, the recommended way to manage OpenRouter keys is now through the web dashboard, which saves them directly to `~/.fcc/openrouter_keys.txt`. The proxy will automatically read from this new file!

